// `file.free_text` hands a buffer back to the allocator this language uses. A
// borrowed `string` did not come from that allocator: `file.read_text` returns the
// C library's buffer, and an owned binding's destructor is what releases an owned
// one. The call used to compile and then die inside the allocator's ownership
// registry with exit 70; the argument's type is what says it cannot work, so the
// rejection happens before the program exists.
int function main() {
    var text = file.read_text("tests/integration/positive/file_owned_annotation/data.txt");
    file.free_text(text);
    return 0;
}
